  "body": "Fork synced at v0.17.0 (branch cut from upstream/main f490458a).\n\n## What changed\n\nFrom the Makera Z1 user report: an Air M7 added in the machine editor was \"ignored on save\", the Carvera post emitted M8 from the seeded Flood, and an operation could not ask for air.\n\n- **Air coolant mode.** `CoolantMode::Air` (\"Air\" in the op page's Coolant picker, `PARAM Coolant air` in the stream, `\"air\"` in project files). `COOLANT_KINDS` (the mounted-machine editor's pick list) gains `Air`.\n- **Every post that reads the ask handles Air.** Fanuc, Fanuc Lathe, Haas, Siemens 840D, Heidenhain, Mazak, Doosan DNM and Tormach Lathe resolve `air` from the machine's `Air` / `Air blast` entry, or refuse it by name (\"operation X: the machine states no air coolant code ...\"). Tormach Plasma already refuses every ask but Off. The Tormach mill post does not read the ask, so the engine's existing `coolantModes` refusal covers it.\n- **`carvera.cps` posts the coolant the op asked for.** It used to take \"first Flood, else first coded entry\", which posted M8 when the seeded Flood was kept. It now declares `coolantModes`. Air takes the `Air` entry. Flood takes the `Flood` entry, failing one a shop's own coded name. A missing match is a named refusal, never a wrong M-code.\n- **The machine's default coolant.** `CoolantMode::machine_default(coolants)` is Flood when the machine can post a flood ask, otherwise the first coded entry's mode. `CreateOperation` starts each new op on its setup's machine's default. On the shipped Carvera (Air M7 only), a new op is Air and posts M7 / M9.\n- **The machine file editor keeps the coolant.** \"Add coolant\" takes the name and the M code together and refuses an empty code by name. Each coolant row has a \"Remove <coolant>\" button, the seeded Flood included. A codeless coolant is a draft refusal that blocks Save and Save As. `save()` now checks the refusals itself, as `save_as()` already did.\n- **`tormach.cps` flood law aligned** with the generic posts. On an Air-only (or Mist-only) list it refuses a flood op by name instead of posting the first coded entry (M7).\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/869-coolant-air.md`.\n\n**Behaviour change (heads-up for the release notes):** an op saved before this change on an Air-only Carvera is still Flood (the old default). It now gets a named refusal telling the user to pick Air, where it used to post M7. New ops on that machine start on Air. A generic post on a machine whose only coolant is named \"Air\" refuses a Flood op the same way; before, it treated \"Air\" as the shop's own flood.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests:\n- `crates/app/tests/coolant_air.rs` (new)\n  - `an_air_only_carvera_starts_a_default_op_on_air_and_posts_m7_m9`: the shipped Carvera, a default op is Air, posts one M7 and one M9, no M8, no warnings.\n  - `an_air_op_posts_the_air_code_not_the_seeded_flood`: Flood M8 + Air M7 on every generic post and the Carvera. The default op is Flood. An Air op posts M7 and never M8. `air_blast` reads as Air.\n  - `an_ask_the_machine_lacks_is_refused_by_name`: Air on a flood/mist machine is refused by name on every post. Flood on the Air-only Carvera is refused by name. The Tormach mill post refuses an Air op, and a Flood op on an Air-only list never posts M7.\n  - `the_machine_default_coolant_reads_the_coded_list`\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/machines_edit.rs::a_blank_mill_swaps_its_flood_for_air_m7_and_keeps_it_through_save_and_reload`: through the real shell, a name-only add is refused by name; Air M7 is added; the seeded Flood is removed; Save As writes the file, which reads back as `[Air M7]` with an Air default.\n- Updated: `machine_edit::a_coolant_code_must_be_a_well_formed_m_word` (an empty code is now refused by name), `coolant_followups::machine_coolant_names_read_through_spelling_variants` (`COOLANT_KINDS` pin), and `carvera_post` (the two-tool pocket stream asks `PARAM Coolant air`).\n\nGate (Linux): `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green (post, app and ui suites; the ui lib holds the new editor test). The gate map does not pick the post-script suites for a `.cps` change, so these also ran green: 44 app suites touching coolant / posts / machines (`coolant`, `coolant_followups`, `coolant_air`, `carvera_post`, `carvera_machines`, `fanuc_post`, `doosan_dnm_post`, `lathe_post*`, `posting`, `conformance`, `smoothing`, `project_roundtrip`, `machine`, `machine_library`, the drilling / probe / mill2d suites, and others). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. First quick run failed on the new UI test: the old one-line \"New coolant ... Add coolant\" row was clipped in a narrow pane, so the click never landed. The add controls now sit on their own grid rows, and the removes are in a wrapped row.\n\n**Goldens:** none moved. `nc/carvera/two_tool_pocket.nc` is byte-identical: its stream now asks for air, and still posts M7 / M9.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The mounted-machine editor window (Setup pane) beyond `COOLANT_KINDS` now listing Air; its \"add coolant\" still adds a codeless Flood row there (it only applies to the mounted machine, never writes a file).\n- Hand test on a real Carvera / Z1.\n- No MCP tool sets an op's coolant today (not added by this PR: it adds no command; `EditOperationParams::with_coolant` predates it). Follow-up filed: #954 (\"MCP: set an operation's coolant\", P1, effort:medium).\n\nChangelog: Coolant: an operation can ask for Air (M7 air blast), resolved from the machine's list or refused by name; a new op starts on its machine's default coolant (Air on the Carvera); the Carvera post posts the op's coolant instead of the first Flood; the machine file editor adds a coolant with its code, can remove the seeded Flood, and never saves a codeless coolant.\n\nCommit type: `feat(post)!` (the BREAKING CHANGE footer covers the Air-only Carvera Flood refusal; under 0.x it bumps MINOR like any feat).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #869\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
